{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791726822431,"sessionID":"ses_ed4c30da5ffeU1tsPBc0oh0Fvg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_9xmK2b9vSJfuukxRWTh32783","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/client_skyrim-theme-transparency/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/client_skyrim-theme-transparency/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: skyrim theme: transparency\n2: \n3: id: client\n4: status: open\n5: analyst:\n6: date: 2026-08-17\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n9: \n10: ## Context (root cause)\n11: \n12: - `static/themes/skyrim/skyrim.css` sets `--color-c-bg: transparent` in `:root` (line 48). Opaque\n13:   values only exist under `html.dark` (lines 88–93).\n14: - Skyrim has `supportsDarkMode: false`, and `src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts` (lines 75–82)\n15:   **removes** the `dark` class for such themes. Under skyrim the `dark` class is therefore never\n16:   present: `bg-c-bg` resolves to `transparent` and all `dark:` fallbacks (e.g. `dark:bg-s-dark-1`)\n17:   are inert.\n18: - Mobile secondary navigations render with `bg-c-bg` → fully transparent drawer over the skyrim\n19:   wallpaper / page content → unreadable.\n20: - Established pattern to copy: theme hook classes with **no** CSS in `src/`\n21:   (`page-container`, `content-container`, `nav-mobile-container`, `nav-desktop-container`) that are\n22:   styled only inside theme CSS files. Skyrim already styles `.content-container` with\n23:   `rgba(14, 14, 18, 0.9)`.\n24: - Affected surfaces (all use `bg-c-bg`):\n25:   - Mobile-only drawers: `SettingsNavigationMobile` (< lg), `TodoNavigationMobile` (< lg),\n26:     `NoteNavigationMobile` (< sm).\n27:   - Dual-purpose panels (absolute overlay on mobile via JS `display:block`, sidebar at larger\n28:     widths): `FeedNavigation` (splits at lg), `TimeTrackingNavigation` (splits at lg),\n29:     `ContactNavigation` (splits at sm).\n30: - NOT affected: `LibraryNavigation`, `FinanceNavigation`, `CalendarNavigation` are desktop-only\n31:   (`lg:flex`, no mobile overlay). The `FunnelButton`/`HamburgerButton` themselves are readable under\n32:   skyrim (`not-dark:bg-c-primary` applies because `.dark` is absent) — out of scope.\n33: - Only `skyrim.css` gets a new rule; all other themes have opaque `--color-c-bg` and need no change.\n34: \n35: ## Task breakdown\n36: \n37: TASK-1: Add a mobile theme-hook class (suggested name: `secondary-nav-mobile-container`, following\n38: the existing `nav-mobile-container` convention) to the three mobile-only drawer navigations.\n39: files: src/lib/components/settings/SettingsNavigationMobile.svelte,\n40: src/lib/components/todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte,\n41: src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte\n42: depends: none\n43: risk: low — purely additive class on elements that are already `display:none` above their\n44: breakpoint (`lg:hidden` / `sm:hidden`); no logic or layout change.\n45: \n46: TASK-2: Add the same hook class to the three dual-purpose navigation panels (mobile overlay +\n47: desktop sidebar in one element).\n48: files: src/lib/components/feeds/FeedNavigation.svelte,\n49: src/lib/components/contacts/ContactNavigation.svelte,\n50: src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte\n51: depends: TASK-1 (use the identical class name)\n52: risk: medium — the same DOM element doubles as the desktop sidebar (≥ lg, or ≥ sm for contacts);\n53: the class itself is inert, but it enables TASK-3, whose rule must stay mobile-scoped or the skyrim\n54: desktop look changes.\n55: \n56: TASK-3: Style the hook class in the skyrim theme with an opaque, theme-matching background, scoped\n57: to mobile widths only (e.g. `@media (max-width: 1023.98px)` to mirror Tailwind's `lg` split, value\n58: suggested `rgba(14, 14, 18, 0.9)` to match `.content-container`).\n59: files: static/themes/skyrim/skyrim.css\n60: depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n61: risk: medium — the media-query breakpoint must match the components' responsive split points;\n62: `ContactNavigation` switches at `sm` (640px), so a single `max-lg` rule would also make its sm–lg\n63: sidebar opaque under skyrim (currently transparent). Decision needed: accept that (arguably better\n64: readability) or add a second `sm`-scoped class/rule. Specificity is fine: the theme stylesheet is\n65: appended to `<head>` at runtime and wins over Tailwind's `bg-c-bg` (proven by the existing\n66: `.content-container` rule).\n67: \n68: TASK-4: Verify — run `npm run check` and `npm run lint`, then manually in `npm run dev`: with\n69: skyrim on mobile widths, open all six navs (settings hamburger, todos/notes/feeds/contacts/\n70: time-tracking funnels) and confirm readability; confirm the skyrim desktop sidebars are unchanged\n71: (still transparent); confirm default theme (light + dark) and at least one other theme are visually\n72: unchanged on mobile and desktop.\n73: files: none\n74: depends: TASK-3\n75: risk: low — verification only; catches regressions in other themes/breakpoints.\n\n(End of file - total 75 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: skyrim theme: transparency\n\nid: client\nstatus: open\nanalyst:\ndate: 2026-08-17\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context (root cause)\n\n- `static/themes/skyrim/skyrim.css` sets `--color-c-bg: transparent` in `:root` (line 48). Opaque\n  values only exist under `html.dark` (lines 88–93).\n- Skyrim has `supportsDarkMode: false`, and `src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts` (lines 75–82)\n  **removes** the `dark` class for such themes. Under skyrim the `dark` class is therefore never\n  present: `bg-c-bg` resolves to `transparent` and all `dark:` fallbacks (e.g. `dark:bg-s-dark-1`)\n  are inert.\n- Mobile secondary navigations render with `bg-c-bg` → fully transparent drawer over the skyrim\n  wallpaper / page content → unreadable.\n- Established pattern to copy: theme hook classes with **no** CSS in `src/`","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/client_skyrim-theme-transparency/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: skyrim theme: transparency\n\nid: client\nstatus: open\nanalyst:\ndate: 2026-08-17\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context (root cause)\n\n- `static/themes/skyrim/skyrim.css` sets `--color-c-bg: transparent` in `:root` (line 48). Opaque\n  values only exist under `html.dark` (lines 88–93).\n- Skyrim has `supportsDarkMode: false`, and `src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts` (lines 75–82)\n  **removes** the `dark` class for such themes. Under skyrim the `dark` class is therefore never\n  present: `bg-c-bg` resolves to `transparent` and all `dark:` fallbacks (e.g. `dark:bg-s-dark-1`)\n  are inert.\n- Mobile secondary navigations render with `bg-c-bg` → fully transparent drawer over the skyrim\n  wallpaper / page content → unreadable.\n- Established pattern to copy: theme hook classes with **no** CSS in `src/`\n  (`page-container`, `content-container`, `nav-mobile-container`, `nav-desktop-container`) that are\n  styled only inside theme CSS files. Skyrim already styles `.content-container` with\n  `rgba(14, 14, 18, 0.9)`.\n- Affected surfaces (all use `bg-c-bg`):\n  - Mobile-only drawers: `SettingsNavigationMobile` (< lg), `TodoNavigationMobile` (< lg),\n    `NoteNavigationMobile` (< sm).\n  - Dual-purpose panels (absolute overlay on mobile via JS `display:block`, sidebar at larger\n    widths): `FeedNavigation` (splits at lg), `TimeTrackingNavigation` (splits at lg),\n    `ContactNavigation` (splits at sm).\n- NOT affected: `LibraryNavigation`, `FinanceNavigation`, `CalendarNavigation` are desktop-only\n  (`lg:flex`, no mobile overlay). The `FunnelButton`/`HamburgerButton` themselves are readable under\n  skyrim (`not-dark:bg-c-primary` applies because `.dark` is absent) — out of scope.\n- Only `skyrim.css` gets a new rule; all other themes have opaque `--color-c-bg` and need no change.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Add a mobile theme-hook class (suggested name: `secondary-nav-mobile-container`, following\nthe existing `nav-mobile-container` convention) to the three mobile-only drawer navigations.\nfiles: src/lib/components/settings/SettingsNavigationMobile.svelte,\nsrc/lib/components/todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte,\nsrc/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte\ndepends: none\nrisk: low — purely additive class on elements that are already `display:none` above their\nbreakpoint (`lg:hidden` / `sm:hidden`); no logic or layout change.\n\nTASK-2: Add the same hook class to the three dual-purpose navigation panels (mobile overlay +\ndesktop sidebar in one element).\nfiles: src/lib/components/feeds/FeedNavigation.svelte,\nsrc/lib/components/contacts/ContactNavigation.svelte,\nsrc/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte\ndepends: TASK-1 (use the identical class name)\nrisk: medium — the same DOM element doubles as the desktop sidebar (≥ lg, or ≥ sm for contacts);\nthe class itself is inert, but it enables TASK-3, whose rule must stay mobile-scoped or the skyrim\ndesktop look changes.\n\nTASK-3: Style the hook class in the skyrim theme with an opaque, theme-matching background, scoped\nto mobile widths only (e.g. `@media (max-width: 1023.98px)` to mirror Tailwind's `lg` split, value\nsuggested `rgba(14, 14, 18, 0.9)` to match `.content-container`).\nfiles: static/themes/skyrim/skyrim.css\ndepends: TASK-1, TASK-2\nrisk: medium — the media-query breakpoint must match the components' responsive split points;\n`ContactNavigation` switches at `sm` (640px), so a single `max-lg` rule would also make its sm–lg\nsidebar opaque under skyrim (currently transparent). Decision needed: accept that (arguably better\nreadability) or add a second `sm`-scoped class/rule. Specificity is fine: the theme stylesheet is\nappended to `<head>` at runtime and wins over Tailwind's `bg-c-bg` (proven by the existing\n`.content-container` rule).\n\nTASK-4: Verify — run `npm run check` and `npm run lint`, then manually in `npm run dev`: with\nskyrim on mobile widths, open all six navs (settings hamburger, todos/notes/feeds/contacts/\ntime-tracking funnels) and confirm readability; confirm the skyrim desktop sidebars are unchanged\n(still transparent); confirm default theme (light + dark) and at least one other theme are visually\nunchanged on mobile and desktop.\nfiles: none\ndepends: TASK-3\nrisk: low — verification only; catches regressions in other themes/breakpoints.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":75,"totalLines":75,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/archive/client_skyrim-theme-transparency/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791726822411,"end":1791726822428}},"id":"prt_12b3da3b40015hgsiGExTLxWFc","sessionID":"ses_ed4c30da5ffeU1tsPBc0oh0Fvg","messageID":"msg_12b3d9be1001yVAUdKZ4vm53l8"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791726822678,"sessionID":"ses_ed4c30da5ffeU1tsPBc0oh0Fvg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_Fhuc8w8yfFkk3pvXXFV89149","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/DATA_LAYER.md","offset":155,"limit":40},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/DATA_LAYER.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n155:   `setCustomApiUrl`/`dropCustomApiUrl`), web → `getPwaApiUrl()` which tries,\n156:   in order: `dev` → `http://localhost:8000`, `PUBLIC_API_URL`, then a\n157:   hostname→API map (`app.solyto.de` → `api.solyto.de`, …) with\n158:   `https://api.solyto.app` as the fallback.\n159: - **`features.ts`** — feature flags (`setCustomApiUrl`, `firstStartupOptions`)\n160:   computed from platform/environment at module load. Read these; do not add new\n161:   ad-hoc flags to components.\n162: - **`navigation.ts`** — the nav item registry: `NavItem` shapes, `navItems`,\n163:   `desktopOrder`/`mobileDefaultOrder`/`mobileVisibleCount`. Syncs with\n164:   `Navigation.svelte.ts` usage tracking.\n165: - **`urls.ts`** — one place for every route deep-link (`urls.todos`,\n166:   `urls.admin.users`, `getDeepLinkUrl`). Routes referenced by `goto()` or\n167:   `<a>` come from here.\n168: - **`themes.ts`** — the theme registry (pure data consumed by the runtime theme\n169:   loading).\n170: \n171: Config files are evaluated at module load; keep them import-light (they are\n172: covered by tests mocking `$env/dynamic/public` + `$app/*`).\n173: \n174: ## `src/lib/types/` — mirror the API, one file per domain\n175: \n176: - One file per domain mirroring the API model: `todo.ts`, `note.ts`,\n177:   `calendar.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `clipboard.ts`, `check_in.ts`, plus auxiliary\n178:   files (`translation.ts`, `api.ts`, `feature.ts`, `platform.ts`, …).\n179: - Type-only imports — `import type { Todo } from '$lib/types/todo'` — keep type\n180:   files out of the runtime graph.\n181: - Two files carry runtime values and are the sanctioned exceptions:\n182:   `src/lib/types/check_in.ts` (tracker/sport constants) and\n183:   `src/lib/types/quick_add.ts` (`CONTENT_TYPE_LABELS`). Everything else in\n184:   `types/` is erased at compile time — if you need a runtime constant, keep it\n185:   in `config/` or in those two files, not scattered.\n186: - Types match the API snake_case fields exactly (`due_at`, `is_completed`,\n187:   `recurrence_frequency`).\n188: - Domain types are used by the store, the components and the `i18n` types; do\n189:   not duplicate a shape elsewhere.\n190: \n191: ## i18n — four locales, typed keys\n192: \n193: `src/lib/i18n/` has exactly four translation tables — `en.ts`, `de.ts`,\n194: `es.ts`, `fr.ts` — typed by `src/lib/types/translation.ts` (`LanguageFile`) so\n\n(Showing lines 155-194 of 229. Use offset=195 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"  `setCustomApiUrl`/`dropCustomApiUrl`), web → `getPwaApiUrl()` which tries,\n  in order: `dev` → `http://localhost:8000`, `PUBLIC_API_URL`, then a\n  hostname→API map (`app.solyto.de` → `api.solyto.de`, …) with\n  `https://api.solyto.app` as the fallback.\n- **`features.ts`** — feature flags (`setCustomApiUrl`, `firstStartupOptions`)\n  computed from platform/environment at module load. Read these; do not add new\n  ad-hoc flags to components.\n- **`navigation.ts`** — the nav item registry: `NavItem` shapes, `navItems`,\n  `desktopOrder`/`mobileDefaultOrder`/`mobileVisibleCount`. Syncs with\n  `Navigation.svelte.ts` usage tracking.\n- **`urls.ts`** — one place for every route deep-link (`urls.todos`,\n  `urls.admin.users`, `getDeepLinkUrl`). Routes referenced by `goto()` or\n  `<a>` come from here.\n- **`themes.ts`** — the theme registry (pure data consumed by the runtime theme\n  loading).\n\nConfig files are evaluated at module load; keep them import-light (they are\ncovered by tests mocking `$env/dynamic/public` + `$app/*`).\n\n## `src/lib/types/` — mirror the API, one file per domain","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/DATA_LAYER.md","text":"  `setCustomApiUrl`/`dropCustomApiUrl`), web → `getPwaApiUrl()` which tries,\n  in order: `dev` → `http://localhost:8000`, `PUBLIC_API_URL`, then a\n  hostname→API map (`app.solyto.de` → `api.solyto.de`, …) with\n  `https://api.solyto.app` as the fallback.\n- **`features.ts`** — feature flags (`setCustomApiUrl`, `firstStartupOptions`)\n  computed from platform/environment at module load. Read these; do not add new\n  ad-hoc flags to components.\n- **`navigation.ts`** — the nav item registry: `NavItem` shapes, `navItems`,\n  `desktopOrder`/`mobileDefaultOrder`/`mobileVisibleCount`. Syncs with\n  `Navigation.svelte.ts` usage tracking.\n- **`urls.ts`** — one place for every route deep-link (`urls.todos`,\n  `urls.admin.users`, `getDeepLinkUrl`). Routes referenced by `goto()` or\n  `<a>` come from here.\n- **`themes.ts`** — the theme registry (pure data consumed by the runtime theme\n  loading).\n\nConfig files are evaluated at module load; keep them import-light (they are\ncovered by tests mocking `$env/dynamic/public` + `$app/*`).\n\n## `src/lib/types/` — mirror the API, one file per domain\n\n- One file per domain mirroring the API model: `todo.ts`, `note.ts`,\n  `calendar.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `clipboard.ts`, `check_in.ts`, plus auxiliary\n  files (`translation.ts`, `api.ts`, `feature.ts`, `platform.ts`, …).\n- Type-only imports — `import type { Todo } from '$lib/types/todo'` — keep type\n  files out of the runtime graph.\n- Two files carry runtime values and are the sanctioned exceptions:\n  `src/lib/types/check_in.ts` (tracker/sport constants) and\n  `src/lib/types/quick_add.ts` (`CONTENT_TYPE_LABELS`). Everything else in\n  `types/` is erased at compile time — if you need a runtime constant, keep it\n  in `config/` or in those two files, not scattered.\n- Types match the API snake_case fields exactly (`due_at`, `is_completed`,\n  `recurrence_frequency`).\n- Domain types are used by the store, the components and the `i18n` types; do\n  not duplicate a shape elsewhere.\n\n## i18n — four locales, typed keys\n\n`src/lib/i18n/` has exactly four translation tables — `en.ts`, `de.ts`,\n`es.ts`, `fr.ts` — typed by `src/lib/types/translation.ts` (`LanguageFile`) so","lineStart":155,"lineEnd":194,"totalLines":229,"truncated":true}},"title":"docs/DATA_LAYER.md","time":{"start":1791726822602,"end":1791726822674}},"id":"prt_12b3da42c001Pa2ZNCRWdaLdme","sessionID":"ses_ed4c30da5ffeU1tsPBc0oh0Fvg","messageID":"msg_12b3d9be1001yVAUdKZ4vm53l8"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791726822773,"sessionID":"ses_ed4c30da5ffeU1tsPBc0oh0Fvg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_bMob3WYUr51JqbHbCgjn6264","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/COMPONENTS.md","offset":130,"limit":60},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/COMPONENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n130: - `todos/views/{ListView,CardView,OverviewView,KanbanView}` and\n131:   `todos/TodoNavigationMobile`, `todos/views/ViewSwitcher`.\n132: - `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, plus `views/{day,week,month}/Mobile*View`.\n133: - Components that switch on screen class read the store once:\n134:   `const viewPoint = getViewPoint();` then branch on `viewPoint.isDesktop` /\n135:   `viewPoint.isMobile` in the markup.\n136: - Name mobile variants consistently: `*Mobile.svelte` or `Mobile*View.svelte`,\n137:   living next to the desktop component they pair with.\n138: \n139: ## Tailwind conventions\n140: \n141: Styling is Tailwind CSS v4 utility classes, theme tokens from the runtime theme\n142: CSS, and dark-mode variants.\n143: \n144: - Use the `c-*` theme tokens for colours (`bg-c-bg`, `text-c-btn`,\n145:   `border-c-neutral-2`, `text-c-danger`, `focus:ring-c-primary`) and `s-dark-*`\n146:   tokens for dark surfaces (`dark:bg-s-dark-3`). Do not hardcode hex colours in\n147:   components.\n148: - Add `dark:` variants where the component needs different colours in dark\n149:   mode.\n150: - Class order is managed by `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss` — write classes and\n151:   let `npm run format`/the formatter sort them.\n152: - Use `size-*` utilities for component sizing (`size-6`, `size-4`) instead of\n153:   mixing `w-`/`h-` where a square is meant.\n154: - Conditional classes via the `class:` directive\n155:   (`class:pt-6={IS_DESKTOP}`) — it composes with plain `class=\"…\"`.\n156: - Utility values that repeat across the app (like the input styling on\n157:   `TextInput`) stay in the shared component, not re-pasted.\n158: \n159: ## Icons\n160: \n161: Icons come from `@lucide/svelte`, imported per-icon from\n162: `@lucide/svelte/icons/<kebab-case-name>`:\n163: \n164: ```ts\n165: import IconLoaderCircle from '@lucide/svelte/icons/loader-circle';\n166: ```\n167: \n168: ```svelte\n169: <IconLoaderCircle class=\"size-6 animate-spin text-c-btn\" />\n170: ```\n171: \n172: No hand-drawn SVGs inline, no icon-font classes; the lucide set is the icon\n173: library.\n174: \n175: ## i18n — `ts.get.*`\n176: \n177: Every user-facing string comes from the translation store:\n178: `const ts = getTranslation();` then `ts.get.layout.save`, or\n179: `ts.get.quick_add.commit_success.replace('%s', destination)`.\n180: \n181: - Never hardcode a UI string in a component. `{ts.get.layout.double_click_to_edit}`\n182:   is the pattern (`Title.svelte`).\n183: - All four locale files (`src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts`) must stay in sync —\n184:   `npm run check` enforces it (`docs/AGENTS.md` hard rule).\n185: - Use `%s`/`%d` placeholders in a translation string and `.replace(...)` at the\n186:   call site when a value is interpolated.\n187: - Translation keys are typed via `src/lib/types/translation.ts`; an invalid key\n188:   is a compile error.\n189: \n\n(Showing lines 130-189 of 280. Use offset=190 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"- `todos/views/{ListView,CardView,OverviewView,KanbanView}` and\n  `todos/TodoNavigationMobile`, `todos/views/ViewSwitcher`.\n- `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, plus `views/{day,week,month}/Mobile*View`.\n- Components that switch on screen class read the store once:\n  `const viewPoint = getViewPoint();` then branch on `viewPoint.isDesktop` /\n  `viewPoint.isMobile` in the markup.\n- Name mobile variants consistently: `*Mobile.svelte` or `Mobile*View.svelte`,\n  living next to the desktop component they pair with.\n\n## Tailwind conventions\n\nStyling is Tailwind CSS v4 utility classes, theme tokens from the runtime theme\nCSS, and dark-mode variants.\n\n- Use the `c-*` theme tokens for colours (`bg-c-bg`, `text-c-btn`,\n  `border-c-neutral-2`, `text-c-danger`, `focus:ring-c-primary`) and `s-dark-*`\n  tokens for dark surfaces (`dark:bg-s-dark-3`). Do not hardcode hex colours in\n  components.\n- Add `dark:` variants where the component needs different colours in dark\n  mode.","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/COMPONENTS.md","text":"- `todos/views/{ListView,CardView,OverviewView,KanbanView}` and\n  `todos/TodoNavigationMobile`, `todos/views/ViewSwitcher`.\n- `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, plus `views/{day,week,month}/Mobile*View`.\n- Components that switch on screen class read the store once:\n  `const viewPoint = getViewPoint();` then branch on `viewPoint.isDesktop` /\n  `viewPoint.isMobile` in the markup.\n- Name mobile variants consistently: `*Mobile.svelte` or `Mobile*View.svelte`,\n  living next to the desktop component they pair with.\n\n## Tailwind conventions\n\nStyling is Tailwind CSS v4 utility classes, theme tokens from the runtime theme\nCSS, and dark-mode variants.\n\n- Use the `c-*` theme tokens for colours (`bg-c-bg`, `text-c-btn`,\n  `border-c-neutral-2`, `text-c-danger`, `focus:ring-c-primary`) and `s-dark-*`\n  tokens for dark surfaces (`dark:bg-s-dark-3`). Do not hardcode hex colours in\n  components.\n- Add `dark:` variants where the component needs different colours in dark\n  mode.\n- Class order is managed by `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss` — write classes and\n  let `npm run format`/the formatter sort them.\n- Use `size-*` utilities for component sizing (`size-6`, `size-4`) instead of\n  mixing `w-`/`h-` where a square is meant.\n- Conditional classes via the `class:` directive\n  (`class:pt-6={IS_DESKTOP}`) — it composes with plain `class=\"…\"`.\n- Utility values that repeat across the app (like the input styling on\n  `TextInput`) stay in the shared component, not re-pasted.\n\n## Icons\n\nIcons come from `@lucide/svelte`, imported per-icon from\n`@lucide/svelte/icons/<kebab-case-name>`:\n\n```ts\nimport IconLoaderCircle from '@lucide/svelte/icons/loader-circle';\n```\n\n```svelte\n<IconLoaderCircle class=\"size-6 animate-spin text-c-btn\" />\n```\n\nNo hand-drawn SVGs inline, no icon-font classes; the lucide set is the icon\nlibrary.\n\n## i18n — `ts.get.*`\n\nEvery user-facing string comes from the translation store:\n`const ts = getTranslation();` then `ts.get.layout.save`, or\n`ts.get.quick_add.commit_success.replace('%s', destination)`.\n\n- Never hardcode a UI string in a component. `{ts.get.layout.double_click_to_edit}`\n  is the pattern (`Title.svelte`).\n- All four locale files (`src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts`) must stay in sync —\n  `npm run check` enforces it (`docs/AGENTS.md` hard rule).\n- Use `%s`/`%d` placeholders in a translation string and `.replace(...)` at the\n  call site when a value is interpolated.\n- Translation keys are typed via `src/lib/types/translation.ts`; an invalid key\n  is a compile error.\n","lineStart":130,"lineEnd":189,"totalLines":280,"truncated":true}},"title":"docs/COMPONENTS.md","time":{"start":1791726822760,"end":1791726822769}},"id":"prt_12b3da4e6001fLqhg3EqHJQLut","sessionID":"ses_ed4c30da5ffeU1tsPBc0oh0Fvg","messageID":"msg_12b3d9be1001yVAUdKZ4vm53l8"}}
