{"type":"text","timestamp":1791726903548,"sessionID":"ses_ed4c30da5ffeU1tsPBc0oh0Fvg","part":{"id":"prt_12b3ed68d001RyoTsgO9o0Whhi","messageID":"msg_12b3ecc8c001yYhi40nZcbTTwZ","sessionID":"ses_ed4c30da5ffeU1tsPBc0oh0Fvg","type":"text","text":"Wrote the task list to `docs/jobs/perform_new-theme-modern/tasks.md`. Summary:\n\n**Branch check:** workspace is on `feature/perform_new-theme-modern` (verified via the worktree `HEAD`), matching `brief.md`. No checkout needed.\n\n**What I found**\n- A theme = a CSS file `static/themes/<id>/<id>.css` + an entry in `src/lib/config/themes.ts`; `ThemeState` injects the theme stylesheet *after* the app CSS, so equal-specificity theme rules override Tailwind utilities (the proven `y2k.css` → `.nav-desktop-container { padding: 0 }` pattern).\n- Nav hook classes: `.nav-desktop-container`/`.nav-desktop` (desktop rail) and `.nav-mobile-container`/`.nav-mobile` (mobile bar). The `p-1` + `rounded-md` on these is exactly what the brief wants removed. `.gradient-down`/`.gradient-right` are used only by the navbars.\n- Theme names are hardcoded (not i18n), and the settings swatch is generated from `preview*` fields — so no component/i18n work is needed. Existing tests (`themes.test.ts`, `Theme.test.ts`) just need to keep passing.\n- Notion research condensed into the context section (warm-neutral palette, Notion blue, system font stack, whisper borders, flat depth, small radii).\n\n**Task list**\n1. **TASK-1** (low) — create `static/themes/modern/modern.css` token set (light, Notion-like). New file.\n2. **TASK-2** (low) — register `modern` in `themes.ts` (`supportsDarkMode: false`).\n3. **TASK-3** (medium) — nav overrides in `modern.css`: flat, flush, square, desktop + mobile.\n4. **TASK-4** (low) — verification (`check`/`lint`/`test` + manual dev-server check).\n\n**Flagged assumption (not blocking):** I scoped dark mode **out** (`supportsDarkMode: false`, matching `paper`/`catppuccin-latte`) and recorded it as an open question in the file — Notion does have a dark mode, so this is the one decision a human may want to reverse. I also documented the interpretation of \"flat bar\" as the existing rail/bottom-bar made flush/flat/square, with a horizontal top bar explicitly out of scope. No new dependencies (Notion uses a system font stack). No renders exist for this job. I did not commit anything.","time":{"start":1791726900877,"end":1791726903542}}}
