{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791729688737,"sessionID":"ses_ed496d16bffeMxk2x8zfnkYdYx","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_ET_LcK23okkoJGibdQq5DWL4151","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/perform_new-theme-modern/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/perform_new-theme-modern/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: New theme: modern\n2: \n3: id: perform\n4: analyst: analyst\n5: date: 2026-10-11\n6: \n7: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n8: \n9: ## Context\n10: \n11: ### What the brief asks\n12: - A new \"modern\" theme that reads like Notion: clean, modern, professional (as opposed to\n13:   solyto's mostly playful themes).\n14: - Navigation must be a **flat bar with no spacing to the border and no rounded border**, on\n15:   desktop **and** mobile.\n16: - Research what makes Notion well designed and copy as much as possible, **fonts included**.\n17: \n18: ### How themes work in this repo (ground truth)\n19: - A theme is two things: a CSS file at `static/themes/<id>/<id>.css` **and** an entry in\n20:   `src/lib/config/themes.ts`. The `id` must match the directory/file name.\n21: - `src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts` `apply()` injects `<link href=\"/themes/<id>/<id>.css\">` into\n22:   `<head>` for every theme except `default` (default is already in the app bundle). The link is\n23:   appended **after** the bundled app CSS, so an equal-specificity theme rule wins the cascade.\n24:   This is the established way theme CSS overrides Tailwind utility classes — proven by\n25:   `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` overriding `.nav-desktop-container { padding: 0 }` over the\n26:   component's `p-1`.\n27: - `supportsDarkMode: false` makes `ThemeState` remove the `dark` class and skip the OS\n28:   colour-scheme listener; the settings \"Appearance\" section is then hidden (`AppSettings.svelte`\n29:   line 61). Light-only themes are the majority (8 of 10) — `paper` and `catppuccin-latte` are the\n30:   clean-light precedents.\n31: - Theme **names are hardcoded** in `themes.ts` and rendered directly in `AppSettings.svelte`\n32:   (`{t.name}`); they are **not** i18n keys. The settings swatch is generated from the `preview*`\n33:   fields. So no i18n and no UI-component work is needed.\n34: - Tests: `tests/unit/config/themes.test.ts` asserts unique ids + hex `preview*` fields;\n35:   `tests/unit/stores/Theme.test.ts` exercises `nord`/`default`. Both must keep passing. CSS itself\n36:   is not unit-tested (there are no component/integration tests).\n37: \n38: ### Navigation DOM — the hook classes to target\n39: - Desktop (`src/lib/components/ui/DesktopNavbar.svelte`, lines 22–25):\n40:   outer `.nav-desktop-container h-full bg-c-bg p-1` → inner\n41:   `.nav-desktop gradient-down flex … rounded-md p-1 … drop-shadow-xl`.\n42: - Mobile (`src/lib/components/ui/MobileNavbar.svelte`, lines 48–50):\n43:   outer `.nav-mobile-container h-full p-1 bg-c-bg` → inner\n44:   `.nav-mobile gradient-right … rounded-md …`; its overflow menu (line 90) is\n45:   `.gradient-down … rounded-lg`.\n46: - `.gradient-down` / `.gradient-right` are used **only** by these two navbars (grep-confirmed), so\n47:   flattening them per-theme only affects the nav.\n48: - These hook classes have **no CSS in `src/`** — they exist purely to be styled by theme CSS (the\n49:   same pattern documented in the archived `client_skyrim-theme-transparency` job).\n50: - The layout constrains the nav: desktop wrapper `hidden h-full 2xl:block`, mobile wrapper\n51:   `block h-16 w-full 2xl:hidden` (`src/routes/+layout.svelte`, lines 134–152). The `p-1` on the\n52:   two `*-container` elements is what currently creates the gap to the window border.\n53: \n54: ### Notion design research (condensed, for the CSS author)\n55: - **Light UI surfaces:** canvas `#FFFFFF`, sidebar/panel `#F7F6F3`, subtle hover; primary text\n56:   `#37352F` (warm near-black), secondary/muted text `#787774`/`#9B9A97`; hairline borders\n57:   `1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.1)` (~`#E9E9E7`).\n58: - **Accent:** Notion blue `#2383E2` (in-app) / `#0075DE` (marketing); pressed `#005BAB`. Semantic:\n59:   green `#0F7B6C`/`#448361`, red `#D44C47`, orange `#D9730D`, yellow `#CB912F`.\n60: - **Typography:** the product UI uses a **system font stack** (SF on Apple, Segoe UI on Windows,\n61:   Roboto on Android, Inter-like on the web) — not a bundled webfont. Body 16px/400/1.5, UI/labels\n62:   500–600, headings 600–700 with slight negative tracking.\n63: - **Depth:** deliberately flat — flat fills, whisper 1px borders, multi-layer shadows with\n64:   cumulative opacity < 0.05.\n65: - **Geometry:** rectangular; small radii (buttons ~4–8px, menus ~8px, cards ~8–12px). Buttons are\n66:   **not** pills.\n67: \n68: ### Interpretation + assumptions (explicit — do not silently change)\n69: - **\"Flat bar\"**: read as making the existing navbar (desktop left rail, mobile bottom bar) flush to\n70:   the window edges (drop the outer `p-1`), square-cornered (drop `rounded-md`) and flat (no gradient\n71:   / no drop shadow). Done in theme CSS scoped to the nav hook classes, desktop and mobile.\n72:   If a *horizontal top navigation bar* was actually meant, that is a structural layout change and is\n73:   **out of scope** here — surface it rather than guessing.\n74: - **Dark mode:** assumed **out of scope** — `supportsDarkMode: false` (light-only), following the\n75:   `paper`/`catppuccin-latte` pattern and the brief's focus on the clean light Notion look. Notion\n76:   does have a dark mode, so adding one (an extra `html.dark { … }` token block) is a clean follow-up,\n77:   but it is not requested. **Open question for the human: should `modern` also support dark mode?**\n78: - **Fonts:** because Notion uses a system stack, **no new `@fontsource` package is needed** (and the\n79:   hard rules forbid installing dependencies without asking). Use a system stack.\n80: - **Do NOT zero the global `--radius-*` tokens** — that is the y2k/atari gimmick and would square\n81:   every card/button/menu. Only the nav bar itself goes square.\n82: - `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` exists but is **not** registered in `themes.ts`; leave it untouched.\n83: \n84: ## Task breakdown\n85: \n86: TASK-1: Create `static/themes/modern/modern.css` with the light, Notion-inspired token set\n87: (warm-white canvas `#ffffff`, sidebar `#f7f6f3`, warm near-black text, Notion-blue accent,\n88: whisper borders, restrained shadows, system font stack) covering the token families other themes\n89: define (`--t-font-body`/`--t-font-heading`, `--color-c-*`, `--color-d-*`, `--color-s-dark*`\n90: overrides so `dark:` utilities stay sane, gray scale as needed, `--t-gradient-colors`) plus an\n91: optional subtle `.logo` filter. Keep normal radii (do not zero `--radius-*`). No nav rules in this\n92: task.\n93: files: static/themes/modern/modern.css\n94: depends: none\n95: risk: low — new file, inert until it is registered in TASK-2.\n96: \n97: TASK-2: Register the theme in `src/lib/config/themes.ts` — `id: 'modern'`, `name: 'Modern'`,\n98: `supportsDarkMode: false`, and four `preview*` hex fields matching the palette; keep `default` as\n99: the first entry.\n100: files: src/lib/config/themes.ts\n101: depends: TASK-1 (the id must match the CSS path `static/themes/modern/modern.css`)\n102: risk: low — pure data; `themes.test.ts` (unique ids, hex preview fields) must still pass.\n103: \n104: TASK-3: Add the modern-theme navigation overrides to `modern.css`: set\n105: `.nav-desktop-container`/`.nav-mobile-container { padding: 0 }` (flush to the border),\n106: `.nav-desktop`/`.nav-mobile` square (no `rounded-md`) and flat (no gradient / no drop shadow) with\n107: themed sidebar/canvas backgrounds, ensuring hover/active nav states stay legible. Cover **both**\n108: desktop and mobile. Decide explicitly what to do with the mobile overflow popover (Notion popovers\n109: are rounded, so leaving it rounded is defensible — state the choice).\n110: files: static/themes/modern/modern.css\n111: depends: TASK-1\n112: risk: medium — relies on the theme stylesheet loading after the app CSS (the established y2k\n113: specificity pattern) and must stay scoped to the nav hook classes so no other theme or surface\n114: changes.\n115: \n116: TASK-4: Verify: run `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`; then in `npm run dev` select\n117: Modern and confirm the palette/typography, the nav is flush + square + flat at desktop (≥2xl) and\n118: mobile widths, hover/active nav states are legible, the Appearance section is hidden (light-only),\n119: and switching back to `default` and one other theme leaves them visually unchanged with no console\n120: errors.\n121: files: none\n122: depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3\n123: risk: low — verification only.\n124: \n125: ## Out of scope\n126: - Structural navigation changes (e.g. converting the desktop rail to a horizontal top bar).\n127: - Dark mode (unless the open question above is answered \"yes\").\n128: - New fonts or any new dependency.\n129: - Registering or modifying the unregistered `y2k` theme.\n130: - i18n changes (theme names are not translated).\n131: - Renders/screenshots (produced by the pipeline, not the developer).\n\n(End of file - total 131 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: New theme: modern\n\nid: perform\nanalyst: analyst\ndate: 2026-10-11\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context\n\n### What the brief asks\n- A new \"modern\" theme that reads like Notion: clean, modern, professional (as opposed to\n  solyto's mostly playful themes).\n- Navigation must be a **flat bar with no spacing to the border and no rounded border**, on\n  desktop **and** mobile.\n- Research what makes Notion well designed and copy as much as possible, **fonts included**.\n\n### How themes work in this repo (ground truth)\n- A theme is two things: a CSS file at `static/themes/<id>/<id>.css` **and** an entry in\n  `src/lib/config/themes.ts`. The `id` must match the directory/file name.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/perform_new-theme-modern/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: New theme: modern\n\nid: perform\nanalyst: analyst\ndate: 2026-10-11\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context\n\n### What the brief asks\n- A new \"modern\" theme that reads like Notion: clean, modern, professional (as opposed to\n  solyto's mostly playful themes).\n- Navigation must be a **flat bar with no spacing to the border and no rounded border**, on\n  desktop **and** mobile.\n- Research what makes Notion well designed and copy as much as possible, **fonts included**.\n\n### How themes work in this repo (ground truth)\n- A theme is two things: a CSS file at `static/themes/<id>/<id>.css` **and** an entry in\n  `src/lib/config/themes.ts`. The `id` must match the directory/file name.\n- `src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts` `apply()` injects `<link href=\"/themes/<id>/<id>.css\">` into\n  `<head>` for every theme except `default` (default is already in the app bundle). The link is\n  appended **after** the bundled app CSS, so an equal-specificity theme rule wins the cascade.\n  This is the established way theme CSS overrides Tailwind utility classes — proven by\n  `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` overriding `.nav-desktop-container { padding: 0 }` over the\n  component's `p-1`.\n- `supportsDarkMode: false` makes `ThemeState` remove the `dark` class and skip the OS\n  colour-scheme listener; the settings \"Appearance\" section is then hidden (`AppSettings.svelte`\n  line 61). Light-only themes are the majority (8 of 10) — `paper` and `catppuccin-latte` are the\n  clean-light precedents.\n- Theme **names are hardcoded** in `themes.ts` and rendered directly in `AppSettings.svelte`\n  (`{t.name}`); they are **not** i18n keys. The settings swatch is generated from the `preview*`\n  fields. So no i18n and no UI-component work is needed.\n- Tests: `tests/unit/config/themes.test.ts` asserts unique ids + hex `preview*` fields;\n  `tests/unit/stores/Theme.test.ts` exercises `nord`/`default`. Both must keep passing. CSS itself\n  is not unit-tested (there are no component/integration tests).\n\n### Navigation DOM — the hook classes to target\n- Desktop (`src/lib/components/ui/DesktopNavbar.svelte`, lines 22–25):\n  outer `.nav-desktop-container h-full bg-c-bg p-1` → inner\n  `.nav-desktop gradient-down flex … rounded-md p-1 … drop-shadow-xl`.\n- Mobile (`src/lib/components/ui/MobileNavbar.svelte`, lines 48–50):\n  outer `.nav-mobile-container h-full p-1 bg-c-bg` → inner\n  `.nav-mobile gradient-right … rounded-md …`; its overflow menu (line 90) is\n  `.gradient-down … rounded-lg`.\n- `.gradient-down` / `.gradient-right` are used **only** by these two navbars (grep-confirmed), so\n  flattening them per-theme only affects the nav.\n- These hook classes have **no CSS in `src/`** — they exist purely to be styled by theme CSS (the\n  same pattern documented in the archived `client_skyrim-theme-transparency` job).\n- The layout constrains the nav: desktop wrapper `hidden h-full 2xl:block`, mobile wrapper\n  `block h-16 w-full 2xl:hidden` (`src/routes/+layout.svelte`, lines 134–152). The `p-1` on the\n  two `*-container` elements is what currently creates the gap to the window border.\n\n### Notion design research (condensed, for the CSS author)\n- **Light UI surfaces:** canvas `#FFFFFF`, sidebar/panel `#F7F6F3`, subtle hover; primary text\n  `#37352F` (warm near-black), secondary/muted text `#787774`/`#9B9A97`; hairline borders\n  `1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.1)` (~`#E9E9E7`).\n- **Accent:** Notion blue `#2383E2` (in-app) / `#0075DE` (marketing); pressed `#005BAB`. Semantic:\n  green `#0F7B6C`/`#448361`, red `#D44C47`, orange `#D9730D`, yellow `#CB912F`.\n- **Typography:** the product UI uses a **system font stack** (SF on Apple, Segoe UI on Windows,\n  Roboto on Android, Inter-like on the web) — not a bundled webfont. Body 16px/400/1.5, UI/labels\n  500–600, headings 600–700 with slight negative tracking.\n- **Depth:** deliberately flat — flat fills, whisper 1px borders, multi-layer shadows with\n  cumulative opacity < 0.05.\n- **Geometry:** rectangular; small radii (buttons ~4–8px, menus ~8px, cards ~8–12px). Buttons are\n  **not** pills.\n\n### Interpretation + assumptions (explicit — do not silently change)\n- **\"Flat bar\"**: read as making the existing navbar (desktop left rail, mobile bottom bar) flush to\n  the window edges (drop the outer `p-1`), square-cornered (drop `rounded-md`) and flat (no gradient\n  / no drop shadow). Done in theme CSS scoped to the nav hook classes, desktop and mobile.\n  If a *horizontal top navigation bar* was actually meant, that is a structural layout change and is\n  **out of scope** here — surface it rather than guessing.\n- **Dark mode:** assumed **out of scope** — `supportsDarkMode: false` (light-only), following the\n  `paper`/`catppuccin-latte` pattern and the brief's focus on the clean light Notion look. Notion\n  does have a dark mode, so adding one (an extra `html.dark { … }` token block) is a clean follow-up,\n  but it is not requested. **Open question for the human: should `modern` also support dark mode?**\n- **Fonts:** because Notion uses a system stack, **no new `@fontsource` package is needed** (and the\n  hard rules forbid installing dependencies without asking). Use a system stack.\n- **Do NOT zero the global `--radius-*` tokens** — that is the y2k/atari gimmick and would square\n  every card/button/menu. Only the nav bar itself goes square.\n- `static/themes/y2k/y2k.css` exists but is **not** registered in `themes.ts`; leave it untouched.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Create `static/themes/modern/modern.css` with the light, Notion-inspired token set\n(warm-white canvas `#ffffff`, sidebar `#f7f6f3`, warm near-black text, Notion-blue accent,\nwhisper borders, restrained shadows, system font stack) covering the token families other themes\ndefine (`--t-font-body`/`--t-font-heading`, `--color-c-*`, `--color-d-*`, `--color-s-dark*`\noverrides so `dark:` utilities stay sane, gray scale as needed, `--t-gradient-colors`) plus an\noptional subtle `.logo` filter. Keep normal radii (do not zero `--radius-*`). No nav rules in this\ntask.\nfiles: static/themes/modern/modern.css\ndepends: none\nrisk: low — new file, inert until it is registered in TASK-2.\n\nTASK-2: Register the theme in `src/lib/config/themes.ts` — `id: 'modern'`, `name: 'Modern'`,\n`supportsDarkMode: false`, and four `preview*` hex fields matching the palette; keep `default` as\nthe first entry.\nfiles: src/lib/config/themes.ts\ndepends: TASK-1 (the id must match the CSS path `static/themes/modern/modern.css`)\nrisk: low — pure data; `themes.test.ts` (unique ids, hex preview fields) must still pass.\n\nTASK-3: Add the modern-theme navigation overrides to `modern.css`: set\n`.nav-desktop-container`/`.nav-mobile-container { padding: 0 }` (flush to the border),\n`.nav-desktop`/`.nav-mobile` square (no `rounded-md`) and flat (no gradient / no drop shadow) with\nthemed sidebar/canvas backgrounds, ensuring hover/active nav states stay legible. Cover **both**\ndesktop and mobile. Decide explicitly what to do with the mobile overflow popover (Notion popovers\nare rounded, so leaving it rounded is defensible — state the choice).\nfiles: static/themes/modern/modern.css\ndepends: TASK-1\nrisk: medium — relies on the theme stylesheet loading after the app CSS (the established y2k\nspecificity pattern) and must stay scoped to the nav hook classes so no other theme or surface\nchanges.\n\nTASK-4: Verify: run `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`; then in `npm run dev` select\nModern and confirm the palette/typography, the nav is flush + square + flat at desktop (≥2xl) and\nmobile widths, hover/active nav states are legible, the Appearance section is hidden (light-only),\nand switching back to `default` and one other theme leaves them visually unchanged with no console\nerrors.\nfiles: none\ndepends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3\nrisk: low — verification only.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Structural navigation changes (e.g. converting the desktop rail to a horizontal top bar).\n- Dark mode (unless the open question above is answered \"yes\").\n- New fonts or any new dependency.\n- Registering or modifying the unregistered `y2k` theme.\n- i18n changes (theme names are not translated).\n- Renders/screenshots (produced by the pipeline, not the developer).","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":131,"totalLines":131,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/perform_new-theme-modern/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791729688583,"end":1791729688722}},"id":"prt_12b695fac001suhM0B2kf081TS","sessionID":"ses_ed496d16bffeMxk2x8zfnkYdYx","messageID":"msg_12b695a04001vy6z0IPgAF80Un"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791729688836,"sessionID":"ses_ed496d16bffeMxk2x8zfnkYdYx","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_ET_GddhUWQ38nDhrEMGd7p48003","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/perform_new-theme-modern/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/perform_new-theme-modern/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ## Summary\n2: \n3: Added a new **Modern** theme to solyto: a clean, professional, Notion-inspired\n4: look as a counterpart to the mostly playful existing themes. It is a light-only\n5: theme (like `paper`/`catppuccin-latte`): white canvas, warm-gray sidebar\n6: (`#f7f6f3`), warm near-black text (`#37352f`), Notion-blue accent (`#2383e2`),\n7: whisper hairlines and restrained multi-layer shadows, all on a **system font\n8: stack** (Notion ships no webfont — SF/Segoe UI/Roboto per platform). The navbar\n9: (desktop rail + mobile bottom bar) becomes a **flat bar, flush to the window\n10: edges, with square corners** — on both desktop and mobile.\n11: \n12: ## Changes\n13: \n14: **TASK-1 — `static/themes/modern/modern.css` (new file).** Token set covering\n15: every family the other themes define: `--t-font-body`/`--t-font-heading`/\n16: `--font-sans` (system stack), `--color-c-*` semantic colors (Notion palette:\n17: blue `#2383e2`, red `#d44c47`, green `#0f7b6c`, yellow `#cb912f`), backgrounds\n18: (white canvas, `#f7f6f3` via the gradient tokens), `--color-d-*` light-blue\n19: surfaces, `--color-s-dark*` remapped to light values so `dark:` utilities stay\n20: sane, a warm Notion gray scale (gray-700 = `#37352f`, the base body text),\n21: `--t-gradient-colors` (flat `#f7f6f3, #f7f6f3`), restrained shadows, an\n22: `html.dark` light-enforcement block (paper pattern) and a subtle `.logo`\n23: desaturation filter. **Radius tokens are untouched** — the whole app keeps its\n24: normal rounded corners; only the nav bar goes square.\n25: \n26: **TASK-2 — `src/lib/config/themes.ts`.** Registered `{ id: 'modern', name:\n27: 'Modern', supportsDarkMode: false, previewBg/previewSurface/previewText/\n28: previewAccent: #ffffff/#f7f6f3/#37352f/#2383e2 }` as the last entry; `default`\n29: stays first. No i18n keys needed (theme names are hardcoded). `themes.test.ts`\n30: (unique ids, hex preview fields) and `Theme.test.ts` pass.\n31: \n32: **TASK-3 — nav overrides in `modern.css`.** Scoped to the nav hook classes\n33: (`.nav-desktop-container`, `.nav-desktop`, `.nav-mobile-container`,\n34: `.nav-mobile`), which are used only by `DesktopNavbar.svelte` /\n35: `MobileNavbar.svelte`:\n36: - `.nav-desktop-container` / `.nav-mobile-container { padding: 0 }` — removes\n37:   the `p-1` gap to the window edge (flush).\n38: - `.nav-desktop` / `.nav-mobile { border-radius: 0; box-shadow: none;\n39:   filter: none }` — square corners, no gradient, no `drop-shadow-xl` (a filter\n40:   utility, hence `filter: none`).\n41: - Bars get the warm-gray `#f7f6f3` fill; hover `rgba(55,53,47,0.06)` / active\n42:   `rgba(55,53,47,0.08)` + `#37352f` text stay legible and match Notion's\n43:   subtle nav fills.\n44: - **Decision, stated:** the mobile overflow popover (`.gradient-down` inside\n45:   `.nav-mobile-container`) stays rounded and is restyled as a Notion menu —\n46:   white surface, 1px hairline border, whisper shadow. The brief's \"flat bar\"\n47:   requirement applies to the nav bar itself, not floating overlays (Notion\n48:   popovers are rounded).\n49: \n50: **TASK-4 — verification.** See \"Known issues\" for the environment-constrained\n51: parts. What was verified:\n52: - `npm run check` → 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n53: - `npm test` → theme tests 20/20 pass (6 failures in `DateHelperExtended` +\n54:   `logic-leaves` are pre-existing — reproduced identically against the pristine\n55:   base `themes.ts`).\n56: - eslint clean on `themes.ts`; new `modern.css` is prettier-clean (repo-wide\n57:   `prettier --check` fails on 494 files pre-existing at the base commit).\n58: - Dev server boots, serves `/themes/modern/modern.css` (HTTP 200), no console\n59:   errors.\n60: - **Playwright verification against the real compiled app CSS + real theme CSS\n61:   + verbatim navbar DOM** (no backend API available, so a static harness):\n62:   - desktop/mobile container padding `4px → 0px` (flush),\n63:   - bar `border-radius 6px → 0px`, `filter: drop-shadow → none`,\n64:     `box-shadow: none`, background `teal/green gradient → #f7f6f3`,\n65:   - active nav `rgba(55,53,47,0.08)` + `#37352f`, hover\n66:     `rgba(55,53,47,0.06)` — legible,\n67:   - body font = system stack, 16px, `#37352f`,\n68:   - mobile popover = white + `1px rgba(0,0,0,0.1)` + 8px radius + whisper\n69:     shadow. Screenshots at `/tmp/opencode-ts/modern-{desktop,mobile}.png` for\n70:     the pipeline.\n71: - Appearance section hidden: `AppSettings.svelte` renders it only when\n72:   `theme.supportsDarkMode` (modern = false); `ThemeState.apply()` drops the\n73:   `dark` class (covered by existing store tests).\n74: \n75: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n76: \n77: - **Production build OOMs in this container** (`npx vite build` is killed\n78:   during the final gzip phase; 1964 modules transform fine). Resource\n79:   limitation of the sandbox, not a code issue — no build errors/warnings\n80:   related to this change.\n81: - **Pre-existing repo failures, not caused by this job:** `npm run lint`\n82:   fails `prettier --check` on 494 files (incl. `themes.ts` at the base\n83:   commit); 6 Vitest failures in `DateHelperExtended.test.ts` (date-sensitive)\n84:   and `logic-leaves.test.ts` (`StatisticWidget` `.bg-blue-50` query) — both\n85:   reproduced unchanged on the base `themes.ts`.\n86: - No backend API in this environment, so the authenticated app (real navbar in\n87:   a live session) couldn't be exercised end-to-end; the CSS cascade was\n88:   verified with a Playwright harness instead (see TASK-4).\n89: - `supportsDarkMode: false` means no dark mode for Modern (per the analyst's\n90:   assumption; adding an `html.dark` token block would be a clean follow-up).\n91: - Mobile overflow popover deliberately stays rounded (Notion menus are\n92:   rounded); only the nav bars are square.\n\n(End of file - total 92 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Summary\n\nAdded a new **Modern** theme to solyto: a clean, professional, Notion-inspired\nlook as a counterpart to the mostly playful existing themes. It is a light-only\ntheme (like `paper`/`catppuccin-latte`): white canvas, warm-gray sidebar\n(`#f7f6f3`), warm near-black text (`#37352f`), Notion-blue accent (`#2383e2`),\nwhisper hairlines and restrained multi-layer shadows, all on a **system font\nstack** (Notion ships no webfont — SF/Segoe UI/Roboto per platform). The navbar\n(desktop rail + mobile bottom bar) becomes a **flat bar, flush to the window\nedges, with square corners** — on both desktop and mobile.\n\n## Changes\n\n**TASK-1 — `static/themes/modern/modern.css` (new file).** Token set covering\nevery family the other themes define: `--t-font-body`/`--t-font-heading`/\n`--font-sans` (system stack), `--color-c-*` semantic colors (Notion palette:\nblue `#2383e2`, red `#d44c47`, green `#0f7b6c`, yellow `#cb912f`), backgrounds\n(white canvas, `#f7f6f3` via the gradient tokens), `--color-d-*` light-blue\nsurfaces, `--color-s-dark*` remapped to light values so `dark:` utilities stay\nsane, a warm Notion gray scale (gray-700 = `#37352f`, the base body text),","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/perform_new-theme-modern/implementation.md","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a new **Modern** theme to solyto: a clean, professional, Notion-inspired\nlook as a counterpart to the mostly playful existing themes. It is a light-only\ntheme (like `paper`/`catppuccin-latte`): white canvas, warm-gray sidebar\n(`#f7f6f3`), warm near-black text (`#37352f`), Notion-blue accent (`#2383e2`),\nwhisper hairlines and restrained multi-layer shadows, all on a **system font\nstack** (Notion ships no webfont — SF/Segoe UI/Roboto per platform). The navbar\n(desktop rail + mobile bottom bar) becomes a **flat bar, flush to the window\nedges, with square corners** — on both desktop and mobile.\n\n## Changes\n\n**TASK-1 — `static/themes/modern/modern.css` (new file).** Token set covering\nevery family the other themes define: `--t-font-body`/`--t-font-heading`/\n`--font-sans` (system stack), `--color-c-*` semantic colors (Notion palette:\nblue `#2383e2`, red `#d44c47`, green `#0f7b6c`, yellow `#cb912f`), backgrounds\n(white canvas, `#f7f6f3` via the gradient tokens), `--color-d-*` light-blue\nsurfaces, `--color-s-dark*` remapped to light values so `dark:` utilities stay\nsane, a warm Notion gray scale (gray-700 = `#37352f`, the base body text),\n`--t-gradient-colors` (flat `#f7f6f3, #f7f6f3`), restrained shadows, an\n`html.dark` light-enforcement block (paper pattern) and a subtle `.logo`\ndesaturation filter. **Radius tokens are untouched** — the whole app keeps its\nnormal rounded corners; only the nav bar goes square.\n\n**TASK-2 — `src/lib/config/themes.ts`.** Registered `{ id: 'modern', name:\n'Modern', supportsDarkMode: false, previewBg/previewSurface/previewText/\npreviewAccent: #ffffff/#f7f6f3/#37352f/#2383e2 }` as the last entry; `default`\nstays first. No i18n keys needed (theme names are hardcoded). `themes.test.ts`\n(unique ids, hex preview fields) and `Theme.test.ts` pass.\n\n**TASK-3 — nav overrides in `modern.css`.** Scoped to the nav hook classes\n(`.nav-desktop-container`, `.nav-desktop`, `.nav-mobile-container`,\n`.nav-mobile`), which are used only by `DesktopNavbar.svelte` /\n`MobileNavbar.svelte`:\n- `.nav-desktop-container` / `.nav-mobile-container { padding: 0 }` — removes\n  the `p-1` gap to the window edge (flush).\n- `.nav-desktop` / `.nav-mobile { border-radius: 0; box-shadow: none;\n  filter: none }` — square corners, no gradient, no `drop-shadow-xl` (a filter\n  utility, hence `filter: none`).\n- Bars get the warm-gray `#f7f6f3` fill; hover `rgba(55,53,47,0.06)` / active\n  `rgba(55,53,47,0.08)` + `#37352f` text stay legible and match Notion's\n  subtle nav fills.\n- **Decision, stated:** the mobile overflow popover (`.gradient-down` inside\n  `.nav-mobile-container`) stays rounded and is restyled as a Notion menu —\n  white surface, 1px hairline border, whisper shadow. The brief's \"flat bar\"\n  requirement applies to the nav bar itself, not floating overlays (Notion\n  popovers are rounded).\n\n**TASK-4 — verification.** See \"Known issues\" for the environment-constrained\nparts. What was verified:\n- `npm run check` → 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `npm test` → theme tests 20/20 pass (6 failures in `DateHelperExtended` +\n  `logic-leaves` are pre-existing — reproduced identically against the pristine\n  base `themes.ts`).\n- eslint clean on `themes.ts`; new `modern.css` is prettier-clean (repo-wide\n  `prettier --check` fails on 494 files pre-existing at the base commit).\n- Dev server boots, serves `/themes/modern/modern.css` (HTTP 200), no console\n  errors.\n- **Playwright verification against the real compiled app CSS + real theme CSS\n  + verbatim navbar DOM** (no backend API available, so a static harness):\n  - desktop/mobile container padding `4px → 0px` (flush),\n  - bar `border-radius 6px → 0px`, `filter: drop-shadow → none`,\n    `box-shadow: none`, background `teal/green gradient → #f7f6f3`,\n  - active nav `rgba(55,53,47,0.08)` + `#37352f`, hover\n    `rgba(55,53,47,0.06)` — legible,\n  - body font = system stack, 16px, `#37352f`,\n  - mobile popover = white + `1px rgba(0,0,0,0.1)` + 8px radius + whisper\n    shadow. Screenshots at `/tmp/opencode-ts/modern-{desktop,mobile}.png` for\n    the pipeline.\n- Appearance section hidden: `AppSettings.svelte` renders it only when\n  `theme.supportsDarkMode` (modern = false); `ThemeState.apply()` drops the\n  `dark` class (covered by existing store tests).\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- **Production build OOMs in this container** (`npx vite build` is killed\n  during the final gzip phase; 1964 modules transform fine). Resource\n  limitation of the sandbox, not a code issue — no build errors/warnings\n  related to this change.\n- **Pre-existing repo failures, not caused by this job:** `npm run lint`\n  fails `prettier --check` on 494 files (incl. `themes.ts` at the base\n  commit); 6 Vitest failures in `DateHelperExtended.test.ts` (date-sensitive)\n  and `logic-leaves.test.ts` (`StatisticWidget` `.bg-blue-50` query) — both\n  reproduced unchanged on the base `themes.ts`.\n- No backend API in this environment, so the authenticated app (real navbar in\n  a live session) couldn't be exercised end-to-end; the CSS cascade was\n  verified with a Playwright harness instead (see TASK-4).\n- `supportsDarkMode: false` means no dark mode for Modern (per the analyst's\n  assumption; adding an `html.dark` token block would be a clean follow-up).\n- Mobile overflow popover deliberately stays rounded (Notion menus are\n  rounded); only the nav bars are square.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":92,"totalLines":92,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/perform_new-theme-modern/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791729688700,"end":1791729688831}},"id":"prt_12b69601a001qSoj4EN3uxz2JQ","sessionID":"ses_ed496d16bffeMxk2x8zfnkYdYx","messageID":"msg_12b695a04001vy6z0IPgAF80Un"}}
